{
  "summary": "Updates the importprunedfunds RPC to accept transactions that spend from the wallet, rather than only those that fund it. It replaces the RPC's manual IsMine check and direct AddToWallet call with AddToWalletIfInvolvingMe, making that method public on CWallet. This ensures transactions that spend wallet outputs without creating new ones are recognized and tracked properly.",
  "problem": "Users of pruned wallets cannot re-import spending transactions if they were previously removed with removeprunedfunds or need manual importing. The RPC checks only IsMine on transaction outputs, rejecting pure spending transactions with 'No addresses in wallet correspond to included transaction' and causing the wallet to report an inaccurate balance.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes open issue #21647 ('RPC importprunedfunds doesn't allow importing spending txs, only receiving txs')",
    "Commit c2da52d366 explains: 'importprunedfunds only accepted transactions that pay the wallet: it checked IsMine and added the transaction directly, so a transaction that only spends the wallet's outputs was rejected'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Exposes CWallet::AddToWalletIfInvolvingMe as a public method to allow backup/RPC code to delegate involvement checking.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Diff provided (previously nopatch); the implementation moves AddToWalletIfInvolvingMe from private to public in wallet.h and adds a functional test case in wallet_importprunedfunds.py.",
  "card": "This PR allows the importprunedfunds RPC to import transactions that spend from the wallet in addition to transactions that fund it. Previously, the RPC checked only transaction outputs with IsMine, preventing users on pruned nodes from restoring spending transactions and causing incorrect wallet balances. The fix routes the import through AddToWalletIfInvolvingMe, which checks both inputs and outputs. This resolves issue 21647 with an accompanying functional test.",
